Ladybird now clamps a cell’s row span to the end of its row group.
Blink clamps a cell’s rowspan to the row count of its section in
ComputeMinimumRowBlockSize(), in table_layout_utils.cc. Gecko keeps
a cell map of its own for each row group, so a span never reaches
into another, and clamps it to the group’s row count in nsCellMap::
ExpandWithCells(). WebKit keeps a separate grid of cells for every
section, filled by RenderTableSection::addCell(), so a span ends with
its section there too. Chrome 158, Firefox 151 and WebKit 26.5 all start
the cells of each tbody in its first column.
